      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Crypt::PBKDF2 versions before 0.261630 for Perl have a weak default algorithm and number of iterations.  The default algorithm is HMAC-SHA1, which should only be used for legacy systems.  These versions default to using 1000 iterations.  Depending on the chosen algorithm, 220,000 to 1,400,000 iterations should be used.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
